<glossentry
    xml:id="papj-term-cross-cutting-concern"
    xml:lang="en-GB"
    xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
    version="5.1">
  <glossterm>Cross-cutting concern</glossterm>
  <glossdef>
    <simpara>
      A concern like <glossterm linkend="papj-term-security">security</glossterm> or <glossterm linkend="papj-term-observability">observability</glossterm> that has no natural boundary within the <glossterm linkend="papj-term-architecture">architecture</glossterm>, but cuts across many components, forcing each to deal with it alongside its primary responsibility — for example, by checking whether a user is allowed access, or by recording an audit trail of its actions for <glossterm linkend="papj-term-legal-compliance">legal compliance</glossterm> and troubleshooting.
      There is no real ‘done’ status to such concerns: they keep recurring as the system or software evolves.
    </simpara>
    <glossseealso otherterm="papj-term-architecture">Architecture</glossseealso>
    <glossseealso otherterm="papj-term-legal-compliance">Legal compliance</glossseealso>
    <glossseealso otherterm="papj-term-observability">Observability</glossseealso>
    <glossseealso otherterm="papj-term-quality-assurance">Quality assurance</glossseealso>
    <glossseealso otherterm="papj-term-security">Security</glossseealso>
  </glossdef>
</glossentry>
